    "body": "> it could potentially useful to do multi stage builds\r\n\r\nI haven't done multi-stage builds before, but I'm open to it.\r\n\r\n> alternatively just build the base image with all the environments and then push that image to docker-hub or the azure pipeline image repo.\r\n\r\nYep, that's what I had in mind.\r\n\r\nFor the time being the base image will be changing _very_ often, so I wasn't sure how we would want to manage it so that changes could be made to the image while making local features testable. Would we keep the `Dockerfile` in this repo? Can we default to using a local image over the remote one? I haven't done a whole lot of Docker, so there's probably a good answer. 😄 ",
